[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:A Puma at Large]
[00:00.84]Lesson 1 | 第1课
[00:02.07]A puma at large | 豹子出逃
[00:04.56]Where must the puma have come from? | 这头美洲狮是从哪里来的呢？
[00:13.42]Pumas are large, cat-like animals which are found in America. | 美洲狮是一种体形似猫的大动物，产于美洲。
[00:18.80]When reports came into London Zoo that a wild puma had been spotted forty-five miles south of London, | 当伦敦动物园接到报告，说在伦敦南面45英里处发现一头野生美洲狮时，
[00:26.08]they were not taken seriously. | 他们并没有认真对待。
[00:28.74]However, as the evidence began to accumulate, | 然而，随着证据的增多，
[00:33.02]experts from the Zoo felt obliged to investigate, | 动物园的专家们感到有必要进行一番调查，
[00:36.86]for the descriptions given by people who claimed to have seen the puma were extraordinarily similar. | 因为凡是声称见过美洲狮的人们所描述的情况竟然惊人地相似。
[00:43.46]The hunt for the puma began in a small village where a woman picking blackberries saw 'a large cat'only five yards away from her. | 搜捕美洲狮的行动是从一个小村庄开始的，在那里，一位采摘黑莓的妇女看见“一只大猫”离她只有五码远。
[00:53.28]It immediately ran away when she saw it, | 她一看到它，它就立刻跑开了，
[00:56.24]and experts confirmed that a puma will not attack a human being unless it is cornered. | 专家证实，美洲狮除非被逼入绝境，否则是不会伤人的。
[01:02.52]The search proved difficult, | 搜寻工作很困难，
[01:04.97]for the puma was often observed at one place in the morning and at another place twenty miles away in the evening. | 因为常常是早晨在一个地方发现美洲狮，晚上却在20英里以外的另一个地方发现它。
[01:12.17]Wherever it went, it left behind it a trail of dead deer and small animals like rabbits. | 无论它走到哪里，身后都留下了死鹿及死兔子之类小动物的痕迹。
[01:18.71]Paw prints were seen in a number of places and puma fur was found clinging to bushes. | 在许多地方都发现了美洲狮的爪印，灌木丛中也发现了美洲狮的毛。
[01:25.00]Several people complained of 'cat-like noises' at night and a businessman on a fishing trip saw the puma up a tree. | 有几个人抱怨说夜里听到了“像猫叫一样的声音”，一位商人在钓鱼时也看见那只美洲狮爬到了一棵树上。
[01:33.73]The experts were now fully convinced that the animal was a puma, | 专家们现在完全相信那只动物就是美洲狮，
[01:38.60]but where had it come from? | 可是它是从哪里来的呢？
[01:40.81]As no pumas had been reported missing from any zoo in the country, | 由于全国任何一家动物园都没有报道说美洲狮失踪，
[01:45.35]this one must have been in the possession of a private collector and somehow managed to escape. | 那么这只美洲狮一定是某个私人收藏者喂养的，且不知怎么设法逃脱了。
[01:51.77]The hunt went on for several weeks, | 搜捕进行了数周，
[01:54.23]but the puma was not caught. | 但那只美洲狮仍未捕获。
[01:56.92]It is disturbing to think that a dangerous wild animal is still at large in the quiet countryside. | 想到在这宁静的乡村里，一只危险的野生动物仍然逍遥在外，真令人不安。
